{"case_id":"T8030","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["entry_point","configuration","input_semantics","state"],"confidence":99,"affected_functions":["simdjson::dom::parser::parse_many","simdjson::ondemand::parser::iterate_many","simdjson::dom::document_stream::iterator::source","simdjson::ondemand::document_stream::iterator::source","find_next_document_index_json_sequence","fallback::scan"],"reason":"H0 does not exercise the changed stream-format protocols. fuzz_ndjson calls parser.parse_many(json,batch_size) only with the default format, while fuzz_ondemand calls parser.iterate(padded) rather than iterate_many. Consequently, neither simdjson::stream_format::comma_delimited_array nor explicit json_sequence processing is selected, and iterator source slicing is not inspected. This misses fuzz-worthy wrapper validation and trimming, stream batching, delimiter handling, consecutive RS records, scalar/string record boundaries, and source-view behavior.","evidence":["S1 adds simdjson::stream_format::comma_delimited_array and new leading/trailing JSON-whitespace plus '[' and ']' handling in both dom::parser::parse_many and ondemand::parser::iterate_many.","H0 fuzz_ndjson invokes parser.parse_many(json,batch_size) without a stream_format argument, so it cannot select comma_delimited_array or json_sequence.","H0 fuzz_ondemand invokes parser.iterate(padded), not parser.iterate_many(..., stream_format), so it does not reach the changed on-demand streaming entry point.","S1 changes both document_stream::iterator::source implementations to trim byte 0x1E for scalar documents, but H0 never calls iterator.source().","S1 changes fallback::scan and find_next_document_index_json_sequence for RS-delimited scalar and string values, consecutive RS bytes, partial/final batches, and structural-index insertion; no H0 input controls stream_format::json_sequence.","The existing fuzz_ndjson state check only repeats default parse_many iteration and compares document and boolean counts; it does not vary stream format or validate source slices and delimiter-specific boundaries."],"recommended_action":"Add streaming harness coverage that derives stream_format and batch_size from fuzz bytes, invokes both dom::parser::parse_many and ondemand::parser::iterate_many, explicitly includes comma_delimited_array and json_sequence, iterates all documents, calls iterator.source(), and stresses empty/malformed array wrappers, JSON whitespace, nested commas, scalar/string records, consecutive 0x1E bytes, and batch-boundary truncation."}
